---
import { tableMarkup } from '../../lib/photography/table-geometry.js'
---
<figure class="mechanism time-figure iso iso-plate" data-theme="light" aria-label="Across time: real captures, alignment, and merging">
  <div class="figure-header"><span>FIG. 02 / TIME</span><span data-figure-title>Four actual observations</span></div>
  <div class="figure-stage">
    <div class="time-panel captures-panel" data-time-panel="captures">
      {[0,1,2,3].map(i=><div><img src={`/photography/frame-${i}.webp`} width="384" height="384" alt={`Actual capture N00${i}, same crop and display settings`} loading="lazy" /><span>N00{i}</span></div>)}
    </div>
    <div hidden class="time-panel table-panel" data-time-panel="table"><Fragment set:html={tableMarkup} /><div class="correspondence-window"><img src="/photography/frame-0.webp" width="384" height="384" alt="Reference detail from N000" loading="lazy" /><img class="corresponding-frame" src="/photography/frame-2.webp" width="384" height="384" alt="Same detail from N002; measured translation is corrected in the aligned state" loading="lazy" /></div><span class="correspondence-label">N000 + N002 · 6× inspection</span><img class="aligned-preview" src="/photography/aligned.webp" width="384" height="384" alt="Actual registered average before residual rejection" loading="lazy" /><span class="aligned-label">Registered average</span></div>
    <div hidden class="time-panel result-panel" data-time-panel="result"><img data-result-image src="/photography/unaligned.webp" width="384" height="384" alt="Actual average before registration" loading="lazy" /><span class="image-stamp" data-result-label>Unregistered average</span><div class="registration-detail"><img data-detail-image src="/photography/unaligned.webp" width="384" height="384" alt="Magnified detail of the same result, with fixed framing" loading="lazy" /></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="figure-arithmetic" data-arithmetic>Same scene. Different positions and noise.</div>
  <div class="figure-footer"><span data-figure-hint>N000 · N001 · N002 · N003</span><span data-step-count>01 / 05</span></div>
  <figcaption>Same 384 × 384 region as Figure 1. Carriers are a teaching fixture; their lift separates observations for inspection.</figcaption>
</figure>
